  "Question": "What is the value of\n\n\\[ \\begin{gathered} 2(81 + 83 + 85 + 87 + 89 \\\\ {}+ 91 + 93 + 95 + 97 + 99)? \\end{gathered} \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1600\\)",
    "B": "\\(1650\\)",
    "C": "\\(1700\\)",
    "D": "\\(1750\\)",
    "E": "\\(1800\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Pair the smallest term with the largest, then work inward. The pairs are\n\\[\n81+99,\\quad83+97,\\quad85+95,\n\\]\n\\[\n87+93,\\quad89+91.\n\\]\nEach pair totals \\(180\\), and the five pairs use all ten terms exactly once. Thus the sum inside the parentheses is \\(5\\cdot180=900\\). Including the outside factor gives\n\\[\n2\\cdot900=\\boxed{1800},\n\\]\nchoice E.",
